{
    "background_story": "Sir Lubber, a gallant knight of the Round Table, was known for his unwavering dedication to King Arthur's code of chivalry. Though not as renowned as Sir Lancelot or Sir Gawain, Lubber's unshakeable loyalty and honor earned him a respected place among the kingdom's defenders. He was instrumental in the quest for the Holy Grail, facing numerous perils and battling fearsome foes alongside his comrades. Lubber's most notable exploit was his solo defense of the castle of Tintagel against a band of ruthless invaders, where he single-handedly held off the enemy until reinforcements arrived. His selfless bravery and unwavering commitment to justice made him a beloved figure in Camelot, and his name became synonymous with the values of the Arthurian era.",
